<resources>
    <string name="kpui_terms_no_abuse_title">No objectionable content or abuse</string>
    <string name="kpui_terms_no_abuse_body">K has no tolerance for objectionable content or abusive users. You may not post anything that is illegal, sexual content involving children, hate speech, threats, harassment, content that encourages violence or self-harm, or scams. Accounts that do can be removed from what K shows, without notice.</string>
    <string name="kpui_terms_public_title">Your posts are public and permanent</string>
    <string name="kpui_terms_public_body">Posts, replies, likes and room messages are public transactions on the Kaspa network. You are responsible for what you post. Deleting a post removes it from K, but nobody can erase a transaction from the network.</string>
    <string name="kpui_terms_reporting_title">Reporting and blocking</string>
    <string name="kpui_terms_reporting_body">Use Report on a post or room message to tell us about objectionable content; a person reads every report. Use Block to stop seeing an account\'s posts and room messages. We can remove content and accounts from the K indexer, which K reads by default.</string>
    <string name="kpui_terms_account_title">Your account and your funds</string>
    <string name="kpui_terms_account_body">Your account is 12 or 24 words kept on your device. We never have them, so we can\'t recover lost ones or reverse a transaction. Posting pays a network fee in KAS, and you are responsible for the funds you hold and send.</string>
    <string name="kpui_terms_warranty_title">No warranty</string>
    <string name="kpui_terms_warranty_body">K is provided as it is, without warranty, and to the extent the law allows we are not liable for losses from using it or from what other users post. These terms are between you and K\'s developer, not Google.</string>
